<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lothair I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">795–<a href="/years/855">855 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Lothair</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lothair I was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a> and Carolingian emperor from 840 to 855. He fought his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> for control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-verdun">Treaty of Verdun</a> in 843 he received the imperial title and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-francia">Middle Francia</a>, a division that marked the breakup of the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lothair-i.jpg" alt="Lothair I" width="272" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lothar_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
